MCHeli Rework ("the Mod") is a rework of MCHeli 1.0.3 by EMB4 for newer versions of Minecraft.
The original MCHeli and its content (models, textures, sounds, definitions and documentation)
belong to EMB4, are not covered by this licence and are not included in this repository or in
the Mod's releases.

1. What you may do

   a. Use. You may download the official releases of the Mod and use them, for free, in single
      player, on servers (including public and paid servers) and in videos and streams.

   b. Modpacks. You may include an unmodified official release in a modpack, on CurseForge,
      Modrinth or elsewhere, as long as the modpack is free to download and credits the Mod.

   c. Read and build. You may read the source code, build it, and run your own builds for
      personal use, testing and development.

   d. Contribute. You may fork this repository to propose changes through pull requests. By
      sending a contribution you agree that it may be distributed under this licence, and under
      any later version of it, as part of the Mod.

   e. Learn. You may study how the Mod works and write your own code based on what you learned,
      as long as you do not copy the Mod's source code into it.

2. What you may not do without written permission

   a. Redistribute the source code, or builds made from it, modified or not, except as allowed
      in 1(b) and 1(d).

   b. Publish the Mod, or a fork of it, as your own project or under another name.

   c. Sell the Mod or charge for access to it, including putting it behind a paywall.

   d. Remove or change the copyright notices or the credits to EMB4 and Fureniku.

3. Content made for the Mod

   Content packs, models, textures and sounds you make for the Mod are yours. This licence does
   not apply to them. The example pack in examples/rework-example-pack is public domain (CC0 1.0,
   see its own LICENSE file).

4. No warranty

   The Mod is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The authors are not liable for any
   damage or loss arising from its use, including lost worlds or corrupted saves. Keep backups.

5. Ending the licence

   If you break these terms, your rights under this licence end automatically. They come back
   if you fix the breach within 30 days of being told about it.

6. Later versions

   The copyright holder may publish new versions of this licence. Each release of the Mod is
   covered by the version included with it.

